# Catalog fragment for the NeTEx <-> DATEX II EV-charging crosswalk (#446).
#
# This does NOT redefine the whole catalog — the mobility pipeline's catalog.ttl
# already declares eona:catalog (dcat:Catalog) with its title/description. This
# fragment only MERGES additional triples into that single shared catalog via the
# default-graph union (rebuild_default_graph unions ALL named graphs):
#   - one extra dcterms:hasPart edge pointing at the alignment resource, and
#   - the alignment resource's title/label so Prez renders it as a member, and
#   - the align: vann prefix binding for Prez curie routing.
# Loaded (local=True) into its own named graph:
#   https://vocab.eona-x.eu/catalog/crosswalk-netex-datex

@prefix dcat: <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix vann: <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/> .
@prefix eona: <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/> .
@prefix align: <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/> .

# Prefix binding for Prez curie routing (so align:netex-datex-ii resolves).
# Prez expects vann declarations on blank-node subjects, not the namespace IRI.
[] vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "align" ;
    vann:preferredNamespaceUri "https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/" .

# Merge the alignment resource into the shared catalog as an additional member.
eona:catalog dcterms:hasPart align:netex-datex-ii .

# Display title/label so Prez surfaces the alignment as a member resource.
align:netex-datex-ii a dcat:Resource ;
    dcterms:title "NeTEx ↔ DATEX II crosswalk (EV-charging)" ;
    rdfs:label "NeTEx ↔ DATEX II crosswalk (EV-charging)" .
